{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 38, "model_name": "stockmark/stockmark-2-100b-instruct", "content": "Raymond III, Count of Tripoli, was a prominent figure in the Crusader states in the Levant during the 12th century. He was born around 1145 and held the position of count from 1152 until his death in 1187. Raymond's reign was marked by significant challenges and conflicts, particularly with the Saracen forces and internal power struggles among the Crusaders.\n\n*This section highlights Raymond's early life and accession to the throne.*\n\nRaymond was the son of Raymond II of Tripoli and Elvira of Castile. His father's death in 1152 led to his ascension as count at a young age. His uncle, William, Duke of Apulia, served as his regent until he came of age. During his regency, Raymond faced the threat of Nur ad-Din, the Zengid ruler of Aleppo and Damascus, who was expanding his control over the Levant.\n\n*This section focuses on Raymond's military campaigns and alliances.*\n\nRaymond's reign was characterized by a series of military campaigns aimed at defending the Crusader states. In 1164, he formed an alliance with the Byzantine emperor Manuel I Komnenos against Nur ad-Din. However, the alliance was short-lived, and the Crusaders suffered a significant defeat at the Battle of Harim, near Antioch. Despite this setback, Raymond continued to resist Nur ad-Din's forces, engaging in numerous skirmishes and attempting to maintain the Crusader states' sovereignty.\n\n*This section details Raymond's death and legacy.*\n\nIn 1187, Raymond III, Count of Tripoli, was killed during the Siege of Tiberias, a pivotal event of the Third Crusade. Saladin, the Ayyubid Sultan, had captured most of the Crusader states, and Raymond's death marked a decisive moment in the conflict. Though he did not live to see the end of the Crusader states in the Levant, his efforts and leadership are remembered as part of the complex and turbulent history of the Crusades. His reign and the challenges he faced reflect the broader struggle for control over the region during the medieval period.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Ray", "logprob": -1.600783348083496}, {"token": "mond", "logprob": -0.00029213930247351527}, {"token": " III", "logprob": -0.00041345154750160873}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.1496041715145111}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.018380669876933098}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -3.40932747349143e-05}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": -0.00010966652916977182}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": -2.777537883957848e-05}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.3758231997489929}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -0.499492347240448}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.10796705633401871}, {"token": " prominent", "logprob": -0.8854391574859619}, {"token": " figure", "logprob": -0.14388003945350647}, {"token": " in", "logprob": -0.17714667320251465}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.046808261424303055}, {"token": " Crus", "logprob": -0.43250954151153564}, {"token": "ader", "logprob": -0.06867680698633194}, {"token": " states", "logprob": -0.29985442757606506}, {"token": " in", "logprob": -3.130551815032959}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.01059136725962162}, {"token": " Lev", "logprob": -0.5264894962310791}, {"token": "ant", "logprob": -0.0011517327511683106}, {"token": " during", "logprob": -0.09532158076763153}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.00018892886873800308}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -0.5292549133300781}, {"token": "12", "logprob": -0.06904657930135727}, {"token": "th", "logprob": -0.0014701997861266136}, {"token": " century", "logprob": -0.03658784553408623}, {"token": ".", "logprob": -0.035111214965581894}, {"token": " He", "logprob": -0.5487249493598938}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -0.5569328665733337}, {"token": " born", "logprob": -0.5963103175163269}, {"token": " around", "logprob": -1.020007848739624}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -0.004434750881046057}, {"token": "114", "logprob": -1.0106487274169922}, {"token": "5", "logprob": -1.15288853645324